  ('respecting-other-peoples-time', 288, 'Stand by the door with your coat on when you say goodbye at a friend''s house, so the goodbye stays sweet and short.'),
  ('respecting-other-peoples-time', 289, 'Jot a short note to yourself after you keep a promise, about how it felt.'),
  ('respecting-other-peoples-time', 290, 'Skip calling the help line during its busiest hour if you can call at a quieter time.'),
  ('respecting-other-peoples-time', 291, 'Show up on time for a friend''s small celebration, since the first few minutes often mean the most to the host.'),
  ('respecting-other-peoples-time', 292, 'Read your message out loud before sending it, and cut any sentence you stumble over.'),
  ('respecting-other-peoples-time', 293, 'Thank everyone for their time at the end of a meeting, by name if the group is small.'),
  ('respecting-other-peoples-time', 294, 'Let a child know the honest time you will be ready to play, and be ready then.'),
  ('respecting-other-peoples-time', 295, 'Thank a farmer at the spring market who got up early to be there.'),
  ('respecting-other-peoples-time', 296, 'Find out what time the host truly wants guests to arrive when an invite says "around" a time.'),
  ('respecting-other-peoples-time', 297, 'Pin the key details, like the time and the address, at the top of a group chat so no one has to scroll for them.'),
  ('respecting-other-peoples-time', 298, 'Decline a meeting where you have nothing to add, and offer a written thought instead.'),
  ('respecting-other-peoples-time', 299, 'Say an honest "I am not sure yet, I will know by Friday" instead of a yes you might take back.'),
  ('respecting-other-peoples-time', 300, 'Move to the back of the bus when it fills up, so more people can get on at each stop.'),
