  ('respecting-other-peoples-time', 350, 'Free up a shared washer or dryer at the laundromat or in your building as soon as your load finishes.'),
  ('respecting-other-peoples-time', 351, 'Get out of bed at the first alarm one morning, and enjoy the calm of an unhurried start.'),
  ('respecting-other-peoples-time', 352, 'Set your phone aside while you write an important message, so it comes out clear the first time.'),
  ('respecting-other-peoples-time', 353, 'Open the right file before you share your screen, so the group sees what they need right away.'),
  ('respecting-other-peoples-time', 354, 'Tell your team the moment a plan changes so no one works on something that is no longer needed.'),
  ('respecting-other-peoples-time', 355, 'Bring your own pen to an appointment so you are ready to sign without asking.'),
  ('respecting-other-peoples-time', 356, 'Ask a friend who is always on time what helps them, and try one of their habits this week.'),
  ('respecting-other-peoples-time', 357, 'Notice one message you received today that was easy to read, and borrow what made it clear.'),
  ('respecting-other-peoples-time', 358, 'Look back on a meeting today and note one thing that helped it end on time.'),
  ('respecting-other-peoples-time', 359, 'Plan a spring visit you promised to an older relative, and put the date on both your calendars.'),
  ('respecting-other-peoples-time', 360, 'Hum a song while you wait in line, and let go of the need to hurry anyone.'),
  ('respecting-other-peoples-time', 361, 'Enjoy how good it feels to walk in early and settled, and remember that feeling the next time you get ready.'),
  ('respecting-other-peoples-time', 362, 'Thank yourself for every clear, kind message you send today, since each one gives someone back a little time.'),
  ('respecting-other-peoples-time', 363, 'Think of a friend whose visits always feel just the right length, and thank them for it.'),
  ('respecting-other-peoples-time', 364, 'Rest tonight knowing that every promise you kept today made someone''s day a little easier.'),
  ('respecting-other-peoples-time', 365, 'Picture tonight the people whose time you respected today, and feel the quiet good of it.'),
  ('making-friends-with-boredom', 1, 'Take one slow breath the next time a quiet moment arrives, and simply let it stay quiet.'),
  ('making-friends-with-boredom', 2, 'Look out the nearest window for one minute and let your thoughts drift wherever they like.'),
  ('making-friends-with-boredom', 3, 'Put a small notebook somewhere you will see it today, ready for any idea that wanders in during a quiet moment.'),
  ('making-friends-with-boredom', 4, 'Ask a friend or family member what they enjoy doing on a slow afternoon, and really listen to the reply.'),
  ('making-friends-with-boredom', 5, 'Notice the very next moment you feel bored today and quietly name it to yourself: this is boredom.'),
  ('making-friends-with-boredom', 6, 'Wait in the next line you join with your phone tucked in a pocket, and look around the room instead.'),
  ('making-friends-with-boredom', 7, 'Daydream on purpose for five minutes this afternoon, eyes soft, with no goal at all.'),
  ('making-friends-with-boredom', 8, 'Jot one idea in your notebook that arrived while you were waiting, however odd or small it seems.'),
  ('making-friends-with-boredom', 9, 'Leave the tablet in the bag on a short car ride with your kids and play "I spy" together instead.'),
  ('making-friends-with-boredom', 10, 'Place a hand on your belly the next time you feel bored and notice whether your breath is fast or slow.'),
  ('making-friends-with-boredom', 11, 'Stand in the yard or on a balcony for three minutes this morning and let the day start without you.'),
  ('making-friends-with-boredom', 12, 'Watch the clouds from a bench or a window and see what shapes they suggest.'),
  ('making-friends-with-boredom', 13, 'Doodle on the back of an envelope for three minutes while the kettle boils, letting your pen go wherever it likes.'),
  ('making-friends-with-boredom', 14, 'Say "I wonder what you will come up with" the next time a child tells you they are bored.'),
  ('making-friends-with-boredom', 15, 'Scan your body from head to toe during a dull meeting and find where the boredom seems to sit.'),
  ('making-friends-with-boredom', 16, 'Notice the next moment your hand reaches for a screen, pause, and count five slow breaths first.'),
  ('making-friends-with-boredom', 17, 'Follow one thought today as far as it goes, from link to link, without steering it.'),
  ('making-friends-with-boredom', 18, 'Invent a short story about the first object your eyes land on in the room, and tell it to yourself in your head.'),
  ('making-friends-with-boredom', 19, 'Play twenty questions with your partner while you wait for a table at a restaurant.'),
  ('making-friends-with-boredom', 20, 'Ask yourself what you were hoping to feel the last time you reached for something to fill a quiet moment.'),
  ('making-friends-with-boredom', 21, 'Wash the dishes tonight with no music, podcast or show playing, just the water and the plates.'),
  ('making-friends-with-boredom', 22, 'Listen to the rain against a window and let your mind wander along with the drops.'),
  ('making-friends-with-boredom', 23, 'Rearrange three things on a shelf at home, then step back and see whether the new order sparks anything.'),
  ('making-friends-with-boredom', 24, 'Spend a quiet Saturday afternoon at home with a roommate, each doing nothing much in the same room.'),
  ('making-friends-with-boredom', 25, 'Describe what you are doing in a dull moment, plainly, as if you were narrating a nature film.'),
  ('making-friends-with-boredom', 26, 'Let the first ten minutes of your bus or train ride be quiet, with nothing in your ears.'),
  ('making-friends-with-boredom', 27, 'Notice what you think about when nothing is asked of you, and jot down the first thing.'),
  ('making-friends-with-boredom', 28, 'Make up a game using only a coin and a sheet of paper, and play one round of it alone.'),
  ('making-friends-with-boredom', 29, 'Teach a child how to play rock, paper, scissors, then invent a fourth move together.'),
  ('making-friends-with-boredom', 30, 'Pause halfway through a dull task and notice what you most want to do instead, without doing it yet.'),
  ('making-friends-with-boredom', 31, 'Sit on a bench outside for five minutes and let the time pass without filling it.'),
  ('making-friends-with-boredom', 32, 'Lie in the grass on a warm summer day and let your thoughts wander as slowly as the afternoon.'),
  ('making-friends-with-boredom', 33, 'Draw a map of an imaginary town on a scrap of paper during a slow afternoon.'),
  ('making-friends-with-boredom', 34, 'Keep a few riddles in your pocket for a dull wait with a friend, and trade them back and forth.'),
  ('making-friends-with-boredom', 35, 'Wonder what your boredom might be asking for today: rest, company, movement or something new.'),
  ('making-friends-with-boredom', 36, 'Say hello to boredom out loud when it shows up, the way you would greet a familiar neighbor.'),
  ('making-friends-with-boredom', 37, 'Let your mind roam while you shower this morning, and see where it ends up.'),
  ('making-friends-with-boredom', 38, 'Give an old sock a pair of button eyes and turn it into a puppet with a funny voice.'),
  ('making-friends-with-boredom', 39, 'Wait at the doctor''s office with your child and play a quiet game of thumb war.'),
  ('making-friends-with-boredom', 40, 'Compare a restful boredom, like a slow Sunday, with a restless one, like a long line, in your notebook.'),
  ('making-friends-with-boredom', 41, 'Fold a basket of laundry in silence and notice how your mind keeps itself busy.'),
  ('making-friends-with-boredom', 42, 'Write down a strange or silly idea that wandered into your head today.'),
