  ('making-friends-with-boredom', 255, 'Recognize a moment today when your mind wandered somewhere pleasant on its own.'),
  ('making-friends-with-boredom', 256, 'Sort the mail slowly at the counter, giving each envelope a moment of plain attention.'),
  ('making-friends-with-boredom', 257, 'Tilt your head back on a park bench and watch the branches sway above you.'),
  ('making-friends-with-boredom', 258, 'Pick one word at random from a book and write a short paragraph that uses it five times.'),
  ('making-friends-with-boredom', 259, 'Turn a long checkout line into a guessing game with your child about how many steps it is to the door.'),
  ('making-friends-with-boredom', 260, 'Think about who you were with the last time you felt bored, and whether that mattered.'),
  ('making-friends-with-boredom', 261, 'Walk slowly through a store you never shop in, looking at the shelves with no plan to buy anything.'),
  ('making-friends-with-boredom', 262, 'Ask a friend what they daydream about, and share one of your own.'),
  ('making-friends-with-boredom', 263, 'Arrange the magnets on your fridge into a picture or a short message for the next person who looks.'),
  ('making-friends-with-boredom', 264, 'Tell your household one thing you would like to try on the next slow evening, and ask for theirs.'),
  ('making-friends-with-boredom', 265, 'Notice whether you feel bored more often when you are hungry, tired or alone, with no judgment.'),
  ('making-friends-with-boredom', 266, 'Repeat a plain word, like "here," silently to yourself for a minute when time feels slow.'),
  ('making-friends-with-boredom', 267, 'Notice how a thought changes shape when you leave it alone for a while.'),
  ('making-friends-with-boredom', 268, 'Imagine a new holiday that celebrates quiet moments, and decide what people would do on it.'),
  ('making-friends-with-boredom', 269, 'Draw a picture together with your partner, taking turns to add one line each.'),
  ('making-friends-with-boredom', 270, 'Explore in writing the difference between being bored and being lonely, in your own words.'),
  ('making-friends-with-boredom', 271, 'Drop the urge to multitask while you wait on hold, and simply listen to the hold music.'),
  ('making-friends-with-boredom', 272, 'Drift through the memory of a favorite place and notice every detail you can recall.'),
  ('making-friends-with-boredom', 273, 'Daydream about a small project, then put the very first step on a sticky note.'),
  ('making-friends-with-boredom', 274, 'Spend a rainy autumn afternoon with your family building the tallest card tower you can.'),
  ('making-friends-with-boredom', 275, 'Follow your breathing while a webpage loads, and notice how impatience feels.'),
  ('making-friends-with-boredom', 276, 'Choose to arrive a few minutes early somewhere today and spend the spare time simply standing by.'),
  ('making-friends-with-boredom', 277, 'Write a page of whatever comes to mind tonight, letting one sentence lead to the next.'),
  ('making-friends-with-boredom', 278, 'Build a little maze for a marble out of books and rulers on the floor.'),
  ('making-friends-with-boredom', 279, 'Suggest a quiet errand with a friend, like returning library books, and let the time together be ordinary.'),
  ('making-friends-with-boredom', 280, 'Remember a dull task you used to dread that now feels easy, and notice what changed.'),
  ('making-friends-with-boredom', 281, 'Remind yourself, when a meeting runs long, that you can sit with the dullness and still be okay.'),
  ('making-friends-with-boredom', 282, 'Watch the steam rise from a warm drink on a cool fall morning and let your thoughts curl with it.'),
  ('making-friends-with-boredom', 283, 'Draft a recipe for a perfect lazy afternoon, with ingredients like "one blanket" and "a pinch of birdsong."'),
  ('making-friends-with-boredom', 284, 'Start the "I packed my suitcase" memory game with your kids at breakfast, each adding one item.'),
  ('making-friends-with-boredom', 285, 'Ask yourself what a quiet moment would look like if you were not trying to fix it.'),
  ('making-friends-with-boredom', 286, 'Gaze at the glow of a lamp for two minutes in a dim room this evening.'),
  ('making-friends-with-boredom', 287, 'Explore the edges of a half remembered dream from last night and let it unfold a little more.'),
  ('making-friends-with-boredom', 288, 'Trace the shadow of a household object on paper in the late afternoon sun, then color it in.'),
  ('making-friends-with-boredom', 289, 'Watch a sunset with your partner or roommate on a spring evening, staying until the last color fades.'),
  ('making-friends-with-boredom', 290, 'Watch how restless boredom changes when you hum quietly for a minute.'),
  ('making-friends-with-boredom', 291, 'Sip a glass of water slowly while sitting still, and let that be your whole activity.'),
  ('making-friends-with-boredom', 292, 'Leave a gap after a conversation ends and let your mind wander over what was said.'),
  ('making-friends-with-boredom', 293, 'Use the fog on a cold winter window to draw a small picture with your fingertip.'),
  ('making-friends-with-boredom', 294, 'Pass a single sheet of paper around the table and let each person fold it once into something new.'),
  ('making-friends-with-boredom', 295, 'Look for the smallest interesting detail in the dullest spot of your day, like a scuffed floor or a plain wall.'),
  ('making-friends-with-boredom', 296, 'Thank the slow bus or the long line, in your head, for giving you a few unplanned minutes.'),
  ('making-friends-with-boredom', 297, 'Look at an old map or atlas and let your mind wander the roads and rivers.'),
  ('making-friends-with-boredom', 298, 'Read the back of a cereal box and come up with a better slogan for it.'),
  ('making-friends-with-boredom', 299, 'Ride along quietly with your teenager on an errand, letting them pick the music or the silence.'),
  ('making-friends-with-boredom', 300, 'Name one thing you would like more of in your life, since boredom sometimes points to what is missing.'),
  ('making-friends-with-boredom', 301, 'Return to the quiet gently if you catch yourself scrolling, with no scolding, just a fresh start.'),
  ('making-friends-with-boredom', 302, 'Sit on the back step on a quiet evening and let your mind travel wherever the breeze seems to be heading.'),
  ('making-friends-with-boredom', 303, 'Tell a pet or a plant about an idea you have had, out loud, just to hear how it sounds.'),
  ('making-friends-with-boredom', 304, 'Follow a young relative''s rules in a game of make believe for ten minutes, letting them lead.'),
  ('making-friends-with-boredom', 305, 'Adjust your posture kindly when you notice yourself slumping with boredom at your desk.'),
  ('making-friends-with-boredom', 306, 'Charge your phone outside the bedroom tonight so the last minutes before sleep stay still.'),
  ('making-friends-with-boredom', 307, 'Daydream about the season ahead, picturing a morning or an evening you would love.'),
  ('making-friends-with-boredom', 308, 'Line up the books on one shelf by the color of their spines for an evening, and enjoy the rainbow.'),
  ('making-friends-with-boredom', 309, 'Show a child how to whistle with a blade of grass on a summer afternoon.'),
  ('making-friends-with-boredom', 310, 'Choose three words that describe how boredom felt on a rainy spring morning.'),
  ('making-friends-with-boredom', 311, 'Observe how a slow summer afternoon feels when you don''t try to fill it with plans.'),
  ('making-friends-with-boredom', 312, 'Enjoy the drift of thoughts that comes while you brush your hair slowly at night.'),
  ('making-friends-with-boredom', 313, 'Make a paper chain from scrap paper on a rainy autumn evening, writing one idea on each link.'),
  ('making-friends-with-boredom', 314, 'Invite everyone at the dinner table to name one thing they noticed during a quiet moment today.'),
  ('making-friends-with-boredom', 315, 'Reflect at bedtime on whether today felt rushed or slow, and which one you would like more of tomorrow.'),
  ('making-friends-with-boredom', 316, 'Make the bed this morning slowly, without any noise in the background.'),
  ('making-friends-with-boredom', 317, 'Lean on a fence or porch railing outdoors and let your mind wander over the view.'),
  ('making-friends-with-boredom', 318, 'Leave a page of your notebook blank on purpose and come back later to see what you want to fill it with.'),
  ('making-friends-with-boredom', 319, 'Hum a lullaby with a child at bedtime and let it get slower and quieter each time around.'),
  ('making-friends-with-boredom', 320, 'Consider which dull moment today you would happily repeat, and why it felt okay.'),
  ('making-friends-with-boredom', 321, 'Hang laundry outside on a breezy day and let the task take as long as it takes.'),
  ('making-friends-with-boredom', 322, 'Paint or color with no plan at all, and let the shapes and your thoughts wander together.'),
  ('making-friends-with-boredom', 323, 'Draw a comic strip of three boxes about something ordinary that happened this morning.'),
  ('making-friends-with-boredom', 324, 'Look out of a window with a child on a winter morning and watch the birds on a feeder or a branch.'),
  ('making-friends-with-boredom', 325, 'Sit on the edge of the bed on a dark winter morning for one minute and notice your first thought.'),
  ('making-friends-with-boredom', 326, 'Wait for the shower to warm up without reaching for anything, just listening to the water.'),
  ('making-friends-with-boredom', 327, 'Hold a smooth stone or shell and let it remind you of places you''ve been or want to go.'),
  ('making-friends-with-boredom', 328, 'Ask yourself "what if?" about one everyday thing, like doors that open sideways, and follow the thought.'),
  ('making-friends-with-boredom', 329, 'Practice a slow tongue twister with your partner while you fold towels together.'),
  ('making-friends-with-boredom', 330, 'Pay attention to how boredom feels in a noisy room compared with a silent one.'),
  ('making-friends-with-boredom', 331, 'Pick the longer way back to your desk on a work break, walking slowly past the same old hallways.'),
  ('making-friends-with-boredom', 332, 'Puzzle over a riddle with no answer, just to enjoy how your mind moves.'),
  ('making-friends-with-boredom', 333, 'Create a new hairstyle for a doodled character, then give them a job and a hobby.'),
  ('making-friends-with-boredom', 334, 'Give a bored child some quiet time in their room with books and blocks while you stay close by in the next room.'),
  ('making-friends-with-boredom', 335, 'Check what your body needs when boredom arrives, and listen for a small answer like water, a stretch or fresh air.'),
  ('making-friends-with-boredom', 336, 'Write one sentence tonight about what a dull moment today felt like from the inside.'),
  ('making-friends-with-boredom', 337, 'Read one line of poetry, then close your eyes and let the words echo and wander.'),
  ('making-friends-with-boredom', 338, 'Turn your morning coffee or tea into a tiny ceremony by adding one new step to it.'),
  ('making-friends-with-boredom', 339, 'Share a lunch break with a coworker with your phones tucked away, talking about anything except work.'),
  ('making-friends-with-boredom', 340, 'Wonder about the relief you feel when you finally reach for something, and what you were relieved from.'),
  ('making-friends-with-boredom', 341, 'Settle into a comfortable chair after dinner and let the evening be uneventful for ten minutes.'),
  ('making-friends-with-boredom', 342, 'Savor the dreamy feeling of a slow, rainy morning before the day begins.'),
  ('making-friends-with-boredom', 343, 'Rename the rooms of your home with grand titles, like the Great Hall for the hallway, and use them for an hour.'),
  ('making-friends-with-boredom', 344, 'Guess the time without looking at a clock, along with your partner, and see who comes closer.'),
  ('making-friends-with-boredom', 345, 'Compare how you feel after ten minutes of daydreaming with ten minutes of tidying, with no right answer.'),
  ('making-friends-with-boredom', 346, 'Hold off on picking a show for a few minutes after you sit down, and let the blank screen stay blank.'),
  ('making-friends-with-boredom', 347, 'Collect your daydreams in a small notebook and see which themes keep returning.'),
  ('making-friends-with-boredom', 348, 'Challenge yourself, in a dull meeting, to think of one small improvement to your workspace and note it later.'),
  ('making-friends-with-boredom', 349, 'Draw faces on your fingertips with a washable marker alongside a child on a rainy day, and put on a tiny show.'),
  ('making-friends-with-boredom', 350, 'Wonder whether the dull moment you are in right now could become a restful one.'),
  ('making-friends-with-boredom', 351, 'Celebrate finishing a dull chore, like paying a bill, by sitting back for one easy breath.'),
  ('making-friends-with-boredom', 352, 'Turn an idle minute in the car wash into a daydream about traveling through a strange, rainy tunnel.'),
  ('making-friends-with-boredom', 353, 'Tap a rhythm on the table during a slow moment and see if it grows into a tune.'),
  ('making-friends-with-boredom', 354, 'Say yes the next time a friend suggests just hanging out with no plan.'),
  ('making-friends-with-boredom', 355, 'Record one thing boredom has taught you about yourself through this challenge.'),
  ('making-friends-with-boredom', 356, 'Bundle up on a winter morning and sit on the front step for three minutes with nothing to do but feel the cold.'),
  ('making-friends-with-boredom', 357, 'Rest on the couch on a snowy afternoon and imagine you are somewhere very warm and very far away.'),
  ('making-friends-with-boredom', 358, 'Flip back through your idea notebook on a quiet summer night and circle the one that still makes you curious.'),
  ('making-friends-with-boredom', 359, 'Make a family list of ideas to try next time someone says "I''m bored," and stick it on the fridge.'),
  ('making-friends-with-boredom', 360, 'Gaze at the pattern of a knitted blanket or a rug on an autumn evening and notice how your mind settles.'),
  ('making-friends-with-boredom', 361, 'Smile at the next slow, boring part of a movie or book, and let it be slow.'),
  ('making-friends-with-boredom', 362, 'Thank your wandering mind tonight for one idea, memory or moment of calm it brought you.'),
  ('making-friends-with-boredom', 363, 'Choose one idea from your notebook and give it ten minutes of play this weekend, with no need to finish it.'),
  ('making-friends-with-boredom', 364, 'Gather your household on a quiet evening and each share one good thing that came from a dull moment this season.'),
  ('making-friends-with-boredom', 365, 'Thank yourself for one moment this season when you stayed with boredom instead of rushing past it.')
) as v(slug, day, task)
